Source-grounded enrichment

When I explicitly initiate enrichment, the system should use verified property information as the foundation.

Possible enrichment tasks include:

* Organizing verified property facts.
* Mapping source claims to appropriate fields.
* Identifying missing information.
* Adding permitted and verifiable location context.
* Improving the presentation of existing property information.
* Identifying inconsistencies that need review.

The system must distinguish between original facts and supplemental information.

For example, nearby amenities may be added only when they can be verified using appropriate sources.

Do not infer school assignments from proximity.

Do not represent straight-line distances as driving distances.

Do not change the actual property address, pet policy, utilities, features, or other material facts to improve marketing performance.

If the system cannot verify supplemental information, it must label it as unverified or omit it from publishable claims.

