20. REQUIRED ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The project should not be considered complete until the following requirements have been verified.

Import integrity

* Original source information is preserved.
* Structured and unstructured details are captured wherever accessible.
* Missing information is explicitly reported.
* No automatic AI rewriting occurs during import.
* No automatic AI enrichment occurs during import.
* No automatic publication occurs during import.
* Source-fetching and recovery do not overwrite original evidence.
* Manual edits and approved publishing content are protected.
* All supported import paths use the common validation contract.

Extension and Orion

* Both use compatible payloads.
* Both capture accessible listing information.
* Both preserve ordinary source text.
* Both report extraction failures and missing data.
* Both submit imports through the shared validation process.
* Neither bypasses source preservation or validation.
* Both have regression tests.

Validation

* Material missing details can be detected.
* Incorrect submitted values can be detected.
* Recoverable omissions can be corrected using source evidence.
* Conflicting information is flagged.
* Unknown values are not fabricated.
* Manual validation performs real source comparison.
* Validation results are traceable.

Enrichment and rewriting

* Enrichment requires explicit user action.
* AI description rewriting requires explicit user action.
* The original source description remains preserved.
* Material source facts are retained or explicitly flagged.
* Unsupported claims are detected.
* Prohibited content is removed without unnecessary loss of valid facts.
* Description length adapts to the available substantive information.
* The result is professional, readable, and property-specific.

Publishing

* Publication is a separate workflow.
* The final description is validated.
* Critical errors prevent approval.
* Human approval is required before publication.
* The published result matches the approved version.
* Changes remain auditable.

